-williams-trio-return-vs-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama 'headed in good direction' for key players to return from injury vs. LSU","description":"Alabama is optimistic about the return of WR Ryan Coleman-Williams, CB Zabien Brown, C Racin Delgatty and DB Terrance Green for its game Saturday vs. LSU.","published":"2026-11-02T18:27:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50359564/alabama-optimistic-return-key-starters-lsu-showdown","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama WR Ryan Coleman-Williams, out vs. Vols, undergoes knee surgery","description":"Alabama star wide receiver Ryan Coleman-Williams underwent arthroscopic knee surgery to repair a meniscus injury, according to ESPN's Katie George.","published":"2026-10-17T19:13:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50202841/alabama-wr-ryan-coleman-williams-undergoes-knee-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama WR Ryan Coleman-Williams won't play at Tennessee","description":"No. 6 Alabama star wide receiver Ryan Coleman-Williams has officially been ruled out of Saturday's game at No. 14 Tennessee.","published":"2026-10-15T12:32:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50185713/alabama-wr-ryan-coleman-williams-knee-tennessee","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama WR Coleman-Williams unlikely to play vs. Vols, says DeBoer","description":"Alabama star receiver Ryan Coleman-Williams is unlikely to play at Tennessee on Saturday due to multiple injuries, according to coach Kalen DeBoer.","published":"2026-10-12T17:17:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50167114/alabama-wr-coleman-williams-unlikely-play-vs-vols-says-deboer","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5141711/ryan-coleman-williams","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Coleman-Williams"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ryan Coleman-Williams","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_Coleman-Williams","description":"American football player (born 2007)","touched":"2026-11-18T13:13:46Z","intro":"Ryan Alexander Coleman-Williams Jr. (né Williams; born February 9, 2007) is an American college football wide receiver for the Alabama Crimson Tide.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Williams was born on February 9, 2007, in Mobile, Alabama, later attending Saraland High School in Saraland, Alabama. He had 88 receptions for 1,641 yards with 24 touchdowns as a sophomore in 2022 and 72 receptions for 1,324 yards with 19 touchdowns as a junior in 2023. He was named the Alabama Gatorade Football Player of the Year and the Alabama Mr. Football both those years, becoming the first two time Alabama Mr. Football winner, and the first sophomore to win the award. A five-star recruit, Williams reclassified from the 2025 recruiting class to the 2024 class. He played in the 2024 Under Armour All-America Game, where he had a touchdown reception. He committed to the University of Alabama to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Williams made his first college start in week one of the 2024 season at age 17, making him one of the youngest players in FBS football. He earned SEC Freshman of the Week honors for his debut performance against Western Kentucky, catching two passes for 139 yards and two touchdowns in the 63–0 victory. Against No. 2 ranked Georgia, Williams caught six passes for 177 yards, including the game-winning 75-yard touchdown in the fourth quarter to lead the Crimson Tide to a 41–34 victory. As a freshman, he finished with 48 receptions for 865 yards and eight touchdowns."}]}}